%N A067192 Composite c such that sigma(c)==2 (mod phi(c)).
%C A067192 If 2^k-3 is prime (A050414), then 2^(k-2)*(2^k-3) is a term. The only known term not of this form is 1332. - _Giovanni Resta_, Mar 29 2020; updated by _Max Alekseyev_, Oct 14 2026
%C A067192 a(15) > 10^24. - _Max Alekseyev_, Oct 14 2026
%o A067192 (PARI) isok(c) = !isprime(c) && ((sigma(c) % eulerphi(c)) == 2); \\ _Michel Marcus_, Feb 17 2021
